<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87992" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόμᾰχ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fighting before</i> or
				<i>in front</i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόμαχοι, οἱ,</span>
			<i>champions,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν προμάχοισι φανέντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.31
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρώτοισιν ἐνὶ π. μιγέντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					18.379
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.354
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προμάχων ἀν᾽ ὅμιλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>I.</u>
					7(6).35
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> as
			Adj., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. δόρυ</span> the
				<i>champion</i> spear, i.e. of Heracles (v. Sch.), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				856
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>fighting for,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόλεως, δόμων,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				419
			</span></i>(lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				482
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεσμῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					3.638
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as a name of
			tutelary gods, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀθηνᾶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					3.51
				</span></i>
			, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρὰ προμάχῳ Παλλάδι</span>
			<u>IG</u>l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἠρακλῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Paus.
					9.11.4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐρμῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					9.22.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			Subst., <i>bastion,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Procop.
				<u>Aed.</u>
				5.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b> in Crete,
				<i>cake</i> made for a seven-days-old child, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ών,</span> later form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προμαχεών,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Je.</u>
				5.10
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				<u>Bel.</u>
				91.50
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				5.4.2
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
